# Auto-generated by opencode-vm — safe to edit; regenerated only if missing.
#
# Why these are ignored:
#   cache/         Incremental-build cache (tree-sitter parses + file hashes).
#                  Can grow to ~10,000 files for medium codebases. Reproduced
#                  automatically by `graphify watch`/`update` — committing it
#                  trades repo bloat for marginal cold-start speedup. Skip it.
#   manifest.json  Tracks mtime per source file. Per graphify upstream, mtimes
#                  are not preserved across `git clone`, so a committed
#                  manifest forces a full rebuild on every fresh checkout
#                  anyway — better to regenerate locally.
#
# What stays committed (and is what agents/humans actually consume):
#   graph.json        — the queryable graph the MCP server reads
#   graph.html        — interactive visualization
#   GRAPH_REPORT.md   — human-readable summary
#   README.md         — this folder's purpose

